# logcheck ignore rules for the water heater monitor
# Install on netwatch as: /etc/logcheck/ignore.d.server/waterheater
#
# ONLY NEEDED IF you add /var/log/remote/waterheater.log to
# /etc/logcheck/logcheck.logfiles — as of 2026-08-21 logcheck does not
# watch that file, so heartbeats are not reaching logcheck reports at all.
#
# netwatch's remote logs use ISO 8601 timestamps (2026-08-21T09:25:11-05:00),
# not the RFC 3164 format the stock logcheck rules assume.
#
# Only HEALTHY heartbeats (flash_code=1) are ignored, so a pilot outage is
# never silenced along with the routine noise.
^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}T[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}[+-][0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2} [._[:alnum:]-]+ waterheater: \[heartbeat\] alive flash_code=1 .*$
